# postpilot — staging api. INERT: `import conf.d/*.caddy` only globs *.caddy, so the
# `.disabled` suffix keeps this out of the assembled config. That is deliberate — the whole
# directory can be copied to a shared box without any risk, and staging is switched on by
# a rename rather than by remembering not to copy a file.
#
# To enable, in this order:
#   1. add POSTPILOT_API_DOMAIN_STAGING=… to /srv/edge/.env
#   2. mv postpilot.staging.caddy.disabled postpilot.staging.caddy
#   3. validate (DEPLOY.md §4), then `docker compose up -d` (the .env change needs a
#      recreate, not a reload)
# Enabling it with the variable unset expands to an empty site address, which Caddy rejects
# — and that rejection drops TLS for every project on the box, not just postpilot.
{$POSTPILOT_API_DOMAIN_STAGING} {
	reverse_proxy postpilot-api-staging:8080 {
		transport http {
			versions h2c 2
		}
	}
}
